---
name: Reduce HarfangLab ECS documents for Elasticsearch
description: |
  Drains the Elastic pull export of a HarfangLab Manager every minute, keeps
  every ECS document in ClickHouse as the data lake, and sends Elasticsearch a
  reduced stream: network connections and URL requests become summaries,
  process starts and library loads pass through once with their repeats
  summarized, and all other documents pass through unchanged.

  The documents go to the data stream `logs-harfanglab-default`, which the
  built-in `logs-*-*` index template creates with `@timestamp` as its time
  field. Summaries arrive up to one window after the documents that they
  count, so searches over them should select by ingest time
  (`event.ingested`). Create the ClickHouse table before you start the
  pipeline, for example with a `JSON` catch-all column.
---

every 1min {
  harfanglab::fetch "https://example.hurukai.io:8443",
    token=secret("harfanglab-api-token"),
    format="ecs"
}
fork {
  harfanglab::ecs::reduce
  to_elasticsearch "https://elasticsearch.example.com:9200",
    action="create",
    index="logs-harfanglab-default",
    user="tenzir",
    passwd=secret("elasticsearch-password")
}
to_clickhouse host="clickhouse.example.com", table="harfanglab_ecs",
  mode="append"
